			"snippet": "The satisfies operator narrows a value without widening the type it was declared with, so the compiler keeps the literal type of the expression while still proving that it matches the shape the constraint requires. It was added in TypeScript 4.9 and it is most useful where a type annotation would erase information the rest of the file still needs, for example when building a configuration object whose keys must stay literal. It was added in TypeScript 4.9 and it is most useful where a type annotation would erase information the rest of the file still needs, for example when building a configuration object whose keys must stay literal."
